usage: janus maintain [-h] [--environment ENVIRONMENT]
                      [--project-root PROJECT_ROOT] [--dry-run | --apply]
                      [--zone {bronze,metadata,lineage,runs-table,raw}]
                      [--source-id SOURCE_ID] [--format {text,json}]

Plan declared retention policies by default, or apply them with recorded
evidence.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --environment ENVIRONMENT
                        Environment profile name under conf/environments
                        without the .yaml suffix.
  --project-root PROJECT_ROOT
                        Project root used to resolve conf/ and data/ paths.
  --dry-run             Print and record the retention plan without deleting
                        anything (the default).
  --apply               Apply the declared retention plan and record each
                        item's outcome.
  --zone {bronze,metadata,lineage,runs-table,raw}
                        Limit maintenance to this zone; repeat to select
                        several. Defaults to all declared zones, with raw
                        included only when enabled.
  --source-id SOURCE_ID
                        Restrict bronze, metadata and raw to these sources;
                        repeat to select several. Shared lineage files and
                        runs-table partitions cannot be filtered by source.
  --format {text,json}  Report format. JSON is exactly the persisted
                        maintenance record.
